{"kind":"event","event_id":8374,"event_uid":"01M2PV84QYHKN2T2H4FRB4M8KQ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":346,"issue_uid":"01M2PV4YH2PCBTAEJHB6NWYHD8","issue_short_id":"yhd8","actor":"impl:1@run-28","hlc_physical_ms":1789620654846,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"553fb80c6d1dfbad5020ac2462d58e32079cfd48d6796184818200fd0f94cfc8","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PV84QXFV54SFF9PAKMNXQ5","author":"impl:1@run-28","body":"Approach: TagsInput.tsx modelled on DueInput.tsx — design-system Input, id `tags-<rowId>`, placeholder `tags, comma-separated`, aria-label `Tags for <todoText>`, layout-only `w-40 shrink-0`. Local useState(tags) + mirror useEffect on [tags]; onChange writes local text only; onKeyDown Enter preventDefault -> setTodoTags(store, rowId, text) (imported from ./storeData, since Store.tsx does not re-export it) -> setText(normalizeTags(text)), passed through unconditionally so the empty clear branch reaches the store. Mount in TodoItem directly after DueInput, before the Delete button. Loosen the three text-input-count pins of type-due-date.test.ts to the #due-<N> ids they meant. type-tags.test.ts is the peer's exam; I do not write it.","created_at":"2026-09-17T04:50:54.845228358Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:50:54.846Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":8375,"event_uid":"01M2PV9DFZHETNA2A82Z1P1ZC8","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":346,"issue_uid":"01M2PV4YH2PCBTAEJHB6NWYHD8","issue_short_id":"yhd8","actor":"exam:1@run-28","hlc_physical_ms":1789620696575,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"99de4cdd7e0ffb749c2511d97c69fd15ee73819bfb30d298cfdda88e6bfad896","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PV9DFWM9W88P9B2H42QFHZ","author":"exam:1@run-28","body":"examiner (task 1, tags box in the row): writing `tests/state-exams/type-tags.test.ts` as the Proof names it, four legs.\n\n(a) [M1] the one top-level `stateExam({…})`, declared first, with exactly the clock/entry/seed/store/action/expected/view/mutant the leg spells — the `type` then `key: 'Enter'` pair on the textbox named `Tags for walk the dog`, `state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json` (already checked in at BASE), the four views, and the mutant that drops row 1's `tags` cell.\n(b) [M2] ordinary `bun:test` blocks over `parse(renderStatic(expected))`: one test per row per pin — exactly one `#tags-N`, `input`/`type=text`/`data-slot=input`, the placeholder, the exact `aria-label`, the exact `value`, and the document-order triple `#due-N < #tags-N < first [aria-label^='Delete ']` with each index asserted `>= 0` first.\n(c) [M3] one test, happy-dom registered inside the body with `unregister()` in `finally` after a 25 ms drain, `TagsInput` reached by computed-specifier `await import(resolve(ROOT, 'client/src/TagsInput.tsx'))` (it does not exist at BASE; a static import would fail the whole file at load), rendered under `Provider` with `storesById: {todos: store}` over `createTodosStore(expected)`, native value setter + bubbling `input` event, `KeyboardEvent('keydown', {key: 'Enter'})`, each inside `await act` — the four steps read in order, ending on `getCell('todos','1','tags') === undefined` and `getContent()` equal to the two-open seed.\n(d) [M4] is the Proof's own `Run:` line (`bun test tests/state-exams/type-due-date.test.ts`). It is not encoded in this file: an exam proves its own claim and never runs another exam, so that leg is graded by the run the driver makes of it.\n\nEvery fixture read and every render happens inside a test body (the state linter's capture child imports this file with `stateExam` and `bun:test` stubbed). Expected red at BASE for one reason: no tags box on the tree.","created_at":"2026-09-17T04:51:36.572087350Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:51:36.575Z"}
