{"kind":"event","event_id":8381,"event_uid":"01M2PVH32T8GZ532XZ475J6AJ5","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":346,"issue_uid":"01M2PV4YH2PCBTAEJHB6NWYHD8","issue_short_id":"yhd8","actor":"exam:1@run-28","hlc_physical_ms":1789620948058,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"653a624478e458061cfad7fb4693cff01de30e18a30c40d1c8fb3fe980b35374","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2PVH32RWBNX03XVTVT9GSS9","author":"exam:1@run-28","body":"examiner: exam written and handed in at `tests/state-exams/type-tags.test.ts` (14 tests). Nothing else on the tree is touched.\n\n**Red at BASE, 2 pass / 12 fail, and every failure reads as the absent implementation:**\n- leg (a) — `act: no element matches role=textbox name=\"Tags for walk the dog\"` (no tags box on the page);\n- leg (b), ten tests — no `#tags-N` in the static render (`toBe(1)` got `0`, `not.toBeNull()` got `null`, and the order test's `tagsAt >= 0` got `-1`, which is why each index is asserted `>= 0` before it is compared);\n- leg (c) — `Cannot find module …/client/src/TagsInput.tsx`.\n\nThe two that pass at BASE are supporting pins, not the implementation: `state-exams/expected/two-todos-second-tagged.json` equals the literal M1 spells out, and the markup's two rows are rows `0` and `1` (the pins below are per row id, so this is what says which ids there are).\n\n**Verified green against a throwaway prototype, then reverted** (`git status` shows only the exam file): 14 pass / 0 fail in 2.92 s, the mutant that drops row 1's `tags` cell killed by leg (a), `bun run lint:state` `0 findings over 26 snapshots and 29 exams` with leg (a)'s `view` in place, `bun run typecheck` clean. Two defects deliberately injected into that prototype, each caught by leg (c) at the step meant to catch it: an `if (text)` guard on the commit fails step four (`getCell` got `\"home,urgent,work\"`, wanted `undefined`), and writing the store from `onChange` fails step two (`getCell` got `\"home,urgent,work\"`, wanted `\"home,urgent\"`).\n\n**One reading worth recording.** Leg (d) [M4] is the Proof's own `Run:` line, `bun test tests/state-exams/type-due-date.test.ts`. It is deliberately **not** encoded in the exam file: an exam proves its own claim through imports and calls and never spawns a test runner or runs another exam, so that leg is graded by the driver's run of that file on this tree — the implementer still owes the three loosened pins there (lines 108 and 129 at BASE), and those are in this task's file scope.\n\nLeg (c)'s `Provider` is handed `storesById: {todos: store}` over `createTodosStore(<expected content>)` — M3's \"a `createTodosStore()` holding the expected content\" read as the seed argument, since leg (a)'s `store: () => createTodosStore()` is the unseeded contrast. `root.unmount()` is wrapped in `act` so a green run prints no React act warning.","created_at":"2026-09-17T04:55:48.056138780Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:55:48.058Z"}
